      <h2>Why Mossley Hill Needs a Period Property Specialist</h2>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p>Mossley Hill is one of Liverpool's best-known suburbs. 3.5 miles southeast of the city centre. Tree-lined avenues running between Sefton Park to the north and Calderstones Park to the east. A 2-bed terrace in L18 sells for around £185,000. A 4-bed detached on Menlove Gardens South can reach £650,000 and up.</p>

        <p>The housing is mostly large Victorian and Edwardian homes. Three and four-storey detached homes on Menlove Avenue (where John Lennon grew up at Mendips). Big semis along Greenbank Road, North Sudley Road and Carnatic Road. Period terraces filling the streets between.</p>

        <p>These homes are 100 to 130 years old. Original plumbing was lead and cast iron. Most has been part-swapped over decades, but the old pipework is still there. A simple dripping pipe at ground floor often starts two floors above, routed by hidden pipe runs.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <p>The school catchment drives strong family demand. Liverpool College, Dovedale Primary, Calderstones School, Sudley Primary. Top-end fittings, new kitchens, several bathrooms are common in the family homes here.</p>

        <p>The area also has a strong student and rental side. The streets near Carnatic Road still carry the legacy of the old University of Liverpool halls. HMOs and pro lets are mixed in with the owners. We handle both ends at the same fixed rates.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
