      <p class="pf-sub">Four steps that protect your property while we're on the way.</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">1</span><div><strong>Find the stopcock and turn it off</strong><p>For any water leak, the stopcock is your first move. In most Mossley Hill semis and terraces it's under the kitchen sink. In larger Menlove Avenue detached homes it's often in a utility room or basement. In split flats it's usually in an airing cupboard. Turn it clockwise to stop all water.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">2</span><div><strong>If you smell gas, get out</strong><p>Don't touch any switches. Open windows as you leave. Call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/gas-escapes" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--orange);font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Then us on 0151 558 0334 once the property is safe.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">3</span><div><strong>No heating? Check the pressure gauge</strong><p>Look at the gauge on the boiler. It should sit between 1 and 1.5 bar. Below 0.5, you can top it up with the filling loop underneath. That fixes about half of all "no heating" calls. If it doesn't, call us.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">4</span><div><strong>Photograph the damage</strong><p>Take photos and video before you start cleaning. Insurance claims need proof. Mossley Hill homes often have period finishes worth backing up in writing. We give you our own fault report with photos too, ready for your insurer.</p></div></div>
